From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi: require MBO_SUPPORT for the FT key re-install path

The block that re-installs PTK/GTK/IGTK on an FT reassociation is guarded by
DOT11R_FT_SUPPORT, but its runtime condition calls IS_MBO_ENABLE(), which only
exists when MBO_SUPPORT is set: rt_config.h includes mbo.h under #ifdef
MBO_SUPPORT, and mbo.h itself is compiled only for MBO_SUPPORT || OCE_SUPPORT.

MBO_SUPPORT is an independent Kconfig option with default n, so enabling MAP
(which selects DOT11R_FT but not MBO) produced

    fsm_assoc.c:3111: implicit declaration of function 'IS_MBO_ENABLE'

Every other user of IS_MBO_ENABLE in the tree sits inside an
#ifdef MBO_SUPPORT block, so MBO-disabled is a supported configuration and
this one spot is simply missing the extra condition.  Guard the block with
both macros: the runtime test already required IS_MBO_ENABLE(), hence the
code could never execute without MBO and behaviour stays identical.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt_wifi/common/fsm/fsm_assoc.c
+++ b/mt_wifi/common/fsm/fsm_assoc.c
@@ -3106,7 +3106,16 @@
 		}
 	}
 #endif
-#ifdef DOT11R_FT_SUPPORT
+/*
+ * This key re-install path is gated on IS_MBO_ENABLE() at runtime, but the
+ * surrounding guard only asked for DOT11R_FT_SUPPORT.  MBO_SUPPORT is an
+ * independent option (Kconfig default n) and rt_config.h only pulls in mbo.h
+ * when it is set, so an FT-enabled / MBO-disabled build failed with
+ * "implicit declaration of function 'IS_MBO_ENABLE'".  Request both here;
+ * without MBO the condition could never be true anyway, so behaviour is
+ * unchanged.
+ */
+#if defined(DOT11R_FT_SUPPORT) && defined(MBO_SUPPORT)
 	if ((pFtCfg != NULL) && (pFtCfg->FtCapFlag.Dot11rFtEnable) && isReassoc
 		 && IS_MBO_ENABLE(wdev)) {
 		struct _ASIC_SEC_INFO *info = NULL;
